--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DashboardsPage.tsx is a manual Grafana dashboard-JSON composer mounted at /power/dashboards. It
owns NO API data source (manifest record id=page:power-user/Dashboards declares dataSources: none —
"renders from navigation values / local state"). Its render tree:
  - Page header: PageTitle(powerDashboards.title) + intro <p>(powerDashboards.intro)
  - <AINLDashboardComposer onApply={handleApplyAiDraft} />  (the opt-in Helix NL→dashboard drafter;
    its own already-shipped P4 parity unit — TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AINLDashboardComposer.* 0031)
  - GlassPanel1 "Manual dashboard JSON editor": PanelTitle(powerDashboards.editor.title) + Textarea
    (placeholder powerDashboards.editor.placeholder, aria-label powerDashboards.editor.label,
    rows=12, spellCheck off) + Copy(powerDashboards.editor.copy)/Clear(powerDashboards.editor.clear)
    buttons disabled when the trimmed JSON is empty + a deterministic amber statusMessage
    (copyEmpty when blank | copyUnavailable when navigator.clipboard absent | copySuccess on write |
    copyFailed on a write rejection — the page never pushes to Grafana; the user pastes the copied
    JSON into the Grafana JSON Model editor)
  - GlassPanel2 "Curated panel catalog": PanelTitle(powerDashboards.panels.title) + intro
    (powerDashboards.panels.intro) + the name-sorted CURATED_DASHBOARD_PANELS (6 install-static
    panels: alerts_count_stat / battery_soc_stat / charging_sessions_table /
    drives_per_day_timeseries / energy_used_per_day_barchart / vehicles_table), each rendered with
    its name (mono cyan) + description, in a responsive grid (web grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2)
  - State persistence: the JSON textarea is persisted to localStorage under the canonical
    'ai.dashboardComposer.draft' key (survives navigate-away + back).
  - handleApplyAiDraft(draft) = setDashboardJson(JSON.stringify(draft.dashboard, null, 2)) — applying
    a Helix draft pretty-prints the proposed dashboard envelope into the editor (propose-only; the
    user still presses Copy).
Faithful, non-narrowing parity (covenant #2/#5) therefore = reproduce the header + BOTH GlassPanels
(editor + catalog) AND host the real AINLDashboardComposer surface (DRY — no re-implementation),
with its onApply wired to copy a draft's pretty-printed JSON into the editor.

