OUTPUT PATH (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/PowerUser/**`. This path IS
a real, compiled project.yml source group in the CURRENT repo: both the iOS `TeslaSync` and macOS
`TeslaSync-macOS` app targets list `- path: TeslaSync/Features` (project.yml L53-56 iOS / L114-117
macOS, createIntermediateGroups, excluding *Tests.swift), and real sibling pages already ship there
(TeslaSync/Features/{Charging,Driving,Maps,System,Telemetry,Trips,Vehicles,VehicleSystems,
Notifications}/*). The page is therefore shipped at the prompt's mandated path verbatim — no
relocation. (NB: the older sibling SqlPlayground log recorded relocating to `Sources/Features/`
because `TeslaSync/Features` did not yet exist at that time; it exists + is compiled now, so this
artifact honors the prompt path directly.) Unit tests ship at the established Features-test home
`apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/PowerUser/**` (project.yml `- path: Tests/Unit`, the same place the
sibling SqlPlaygroundPageModelTests lives — co-located *Tests.swift under TeslaSync/Features are
excluded from the app target AND not picked up by any test bundle, so the runnable home is
Tests/Unit). Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings`
(an allowed file). Both files compile into the one `TeslaSync` module, so the page shares the
TS*/AINLDashboardComposer/AppRoute symbols with the rest of the app.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/power/dashboards` is nested. A dedicated `.powerDashboards` AppRoute
case is added (pathSegment `power/dashboards` → `.path` `/power/dashboards` matching web exactly;
System group alongside the sibling power-user `.powerSql`/`.powerUser`; SF Symbol
`rectangle.grid.2x2.fill` for the dashboard-grid surface), `AppRouteParser` aliases
`/power/dashboards` → `.powerDashboards` (REQUIRED — the generic first-segment fallback splits on
'/' and would resolve the segment `power`, which matches no route, returning nil), and
`DashboardsRouteRegistration` hosts the page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right
after `SqlPlaygroundRouteRegistration`. So the page is reachable via the System-group sidebar entry
and any `/power/dashboards` deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

