DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DashboardsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
DashboardsPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the page's 13 web i18n keys, the JSON
editor draft (persisted via an injectable DashboardDraftStore — the web localStorage
'ai.dashboardComposer.draft' parity), the Copy/Clear/status logic over an injectable DashboardClipboard
(success / unavailable / failed — all four web branches), the name-sorted 6-panel curated catalog, and a
lazily-cached NLDashboardComposerModel whose onApply pretty-prints a Helix-proposed dashboard envelope
into the editor (web handleApplyAiDraft → JSON.stringify(draft.dashboard, null, 2), propose-only). The
view reproduces every web region — the header (title + intro), the hosted already-shipped
AINLDashboardComposer Helix drafter (reused, not re-implemented — DRY — with all its states), and both
GlassPanels (the manual JSON editor textarea + Copy/Clear + deterministic status, and the curated catalog
with an adaptive column grid). A dedicated `.powerDashboards` route (pathSegment `power/dashboards`,
System group) + parser alias + registration make it sidebar-reachable and `/power/dashboards`
deep-linkable, preserving every RouteTests invariant. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6
strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, incl. previews) and the executed model + route
harness (44/44) + the shimmed XCTest type-check. The full xcodebuild scheme was NOT run — it is gated on
the out-of-scope, P1-owned KMP `Shared.xcframework` Gradle staging (the app module imports `Shared`;
staging OOM-kills this shared parallel-slot host per the sibling logs), and triggering it would be
irresponsible on a shared runner; deferred to its owner / the P99 integration gate.

